+## Exact dominance reduction and independent components
 
-Disconnected components are independent MWIS subproblems. This split is exact because no conflict edge is cut.+Before splitting the graph, remove a contact only if another contact of the same satellite has at least its weight and no additional conflicts with other satellites. Because contacts of each satellite form a clique, replacing the removed contact by its witness preserves feasibility and cannot decrease the objective. Equivalent contacts retain the smallest slot identifier. Repeat until no removal is possible, then split the reduced graph into connected components. This reduction preserves the optimum but can change component boundaries.
